      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"complexities\" in Nigeria often relate to infrastructural challenges, such as inconsistent power supply and logistics, which can impact production timelines. Contract enforcement can sometimes face delays due to bureaucratic hurdles or evolving local business practices, which differs from the more structured approach often seen in Vietnam. While Nigerian work ethic is undoubtedly strong, overall operational consistency can be less predictable than the established, export-focused manufacturing environments you might find in Vietnam.",
